# EEF-CVE-2026-53425 / Missing InResponseTo validation in Samly
# EEF-CVE-2026-53424 / Missing one-time-use enforcement / SAML replay
#
# samly 1.4.0 is still the latest Hex release, and both advisories list
# every release from 0.3.0 as affected, so there is no patched package
# to upgrade to. hex.audit reports these as EEF-CVE ids (aka CVE-2026-53425
# / CVE-2026-53424); no GHSA aliases are published.
#
# web-ng's live SAML ACS path is the custom controller/strategy, not
# Samly.SPHandler:
# - lib/serviceradar_web_ng_web/controllers/saml_controller.ex
# - lib/serviceradar_web_ng_web/auth/saml_strategy.ex
# That path validates signature, audience, recipient, issuer, and
# assertion time window, plus a RelayState CSRF token. It does not
# persist AuthnRequest IDs or compare InResponseTo, and it does not
# record assertion IDs to reject replays. Keep this waiver until
# upstream publishes a patched samly or those checks are added here.
EEF-CVE-2026-53425
EEF-CVE-2026-53424

# GHSA-4g2h-vm7x-747c / esaml XXE
#
# web-ng does not rely on default external-entity expansion in the SAML flow.
# Its local parsing paths explicitly disable external entities and DTD nodes:
# - lib/serviceradar_web_ng_web/controllers/saml_controller.ex
# - lib/serviceradar_web_ng_web/auth/saml_strategy.ex
#
# There is no newer Hex release than esaml 4.6.0 available to upgrade to at
# this time, so we track the advisory here until upstream publishes a patched
# package or the dependency is replaced.
GHSA-4g2h-vm7x-747c

# EEF-CVE-2026-53424 (CRITICAL) / EEF-CVE-2026-53425 (HIGH) / samly 1.4.0
#
# 53424 is Samly.Helper.decode_idp_auth_resp/3 never supplying esaml's
# DuplicateFun, so bearer assertions can be replayed. 53425 is
# Samly.SPHandler.validate_authresp/3 never checking InResponseTo against a
# persisted AuthnRequest ID. web-ng's ACS is
# ServiceRadarWebNGWeb.SAMLController, which does not call those functions.
#
# Hex has no release newer than 1.4.0; the advisories list every 0.3.0+ as
# affected. Keep this waiver until upstream publishes a patched package or
# samly is removed from this Mix project.
EEF-CVE-2026-53424
EEF-CVE-2026-53425

# GHSA-rhv4-8758-jx7v / Decimal unbounded exponent DoS
#
# web-ng currently receives Decimal through shared Ash, Ecto, Postgrex, ADBC,
# and schema tooling dependencies that constrain Decimal to the 2.x line. The
# first advisory-listed patched release is Decimal 3.0.0, so this cannot be
# resolved in this Mix project without a broader dependency compatibility
# upgrade across the Elixir workspace.
#
# Keep this waiver local to this quality gate until the shared dependency graph
# accepts Decimal 3.x or the dependency is otherwise removed from this release.
GHSA-rhv4-8758-jx7v

